---
import AppLayout from '../../../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import { idPhotoStudio, appPath, studio, supportLink } from '../../../../data/apps';

const path = appPath(idPhotoStudio);
const deletionEmail = supportLink('ID Photo Studio data deletion request');
---

<AppLayout
  title="ID Photo Studio Data Deletion | AppCrazy Labs"
  description="Delete ID Photo Studio projects and saved files on your device, or request deletion of support and eligible RevenueCat data."
  canonicalPath={`${path}data-deletion/`}
  heading="ID Photo Studio data deletion"
  kicker="AppCrazy Labs · Privacy & support"
  deck="What you can remove yourself, what we can help delete, and what other services control."
  backLabel={idPhotoStudio.name}
  backHref={path}
>
  <div slot="meta" class="hero-actions">
    <a class="button button-primary" href={deletionEmail}>Email a deletion request ↗</a>
    <a class="text-link" href={`${path}privacy/`}>Privacy policy →</a>
  </div>

  <p>
    <strong>ID Photo Studio has no user account to close.</strong> It keeps photos,
    projects, edits and generated files on your device, not on AppCrazy Labs servers.
    RevenueCat does create a technical customer identifier for purchases, and you may
    also have sent us a support email. This page explains each kind of data.
  </p>

  <section id="device" aria-labelledby="device-title">
    <h2 id="device-title">Delete files on your device</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Delete a project in ID Photo Studio to remove its app-managed original, working
        photo, preview and generated files when they are not used by another project.
        If a file could not be removed, the app tells you and Settings offers cleanup
        for unused local files.
      </li>
      <li>
        To remove all app-managed projects, files and local free-export or ad-reward
        credits, use Android’s clear-storage control or uninstall the app. This may
        reset free export credits; it does not cancel or refund a Pro purchase.
      </li>
      <li>
        Delete separately saved JPEG, PNG or PDF exports in the folder, gallery or file
        manager where you saved them. Project deletion and uninstalling do not remove
        those copies. Delete shared copies or cloud backups through the receiving app
        or backup provider.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      We cannot remotely access or delete local photos or files. Normal use of the app
      does not upload them to our servers. A photo you voluntarily attached to a support
      email is different and can be included in a request to us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="request" aria-labelledby="request-title">
    <h2 id="request-title">Request deletion from us</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Email <a href={deletionEmail}>{studio.email}</a> with the subject
        “ID Photo Studio data deletion request”. The button above starts the email.
      </li>
      <li>
        Tell us whether you want us to delete support correspondence, eligible
        RevenueCat customer and entitlement data, or both. If you previously contacted
        support, write from the same email address if possible.
      </li>
      <li>
        If your request concerns a purchase, include a Google Play order reference or
        RevenueCat app user identifier if you already have it. You can still ask if you
        do not have either; we will explain what is needed to locate the record.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Do not send passwords, payment card details, identity documents or sensitive
      photos. We may ask for limited additional information to verify a record belongs
      to you. We will review the request without undue delay and respond within any
      applicable legal deadline, explaining what we deleted or why something must remain.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="records" aria-labelledby="records-title">
    <h2 id="records-title">Records we can review for deletion</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Support interactions:</strong> emails, contact details and attachments
        you chose to send us, subject to any necessary follow-up or legal retention.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>RevenueCat records we manage:</strong> an anonymous technical app user
        identifier, purchase and entitlement history, and any associated customer
        information, where present and eligible for deletion. This identifier is not
        an ID Photo Studio sign-in account.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Deleting a RevenueCat record can affect recognition or restoration of Lifetime
      Pro. It does not itself refund a purchase or erase Google Play’s order history.
      Continued use or a purchase restore may create a new RevenueCat record.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="other-services" aria-labelledby="other-services-title">
    <h2 id="other-services-title">Records held by Google and others</h2>
    <p>
      Google Play controls its own payment and transaction records. A request to us
      cannot delete those records; use your Google account and Google Play support for
      requests about them. Google AdMob and its advertising partners manage ad-related
      data under their own policies. The app offers ad privacy options where required,
      and Android offers advertising controls. See the{' '}
      <a href={`${path}privacy/#ads`}>advertising section of the privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention" aria-labelledby="retention-title">
    <h2 id="retention-title">What may remain, and for how long</h2>
    <p>
      We keep support information while needed to handle the request and follow-up.
      We or our service providers may need to retain limited transaction or support
      records for a dispute, fraud prevention, accounting, tax or another legal
      obligation. Eligible RevenueCat data is deleted after a verified request, subject
      to those requirements. Google Play and AdMob apply their own retention policies
      to records under their control.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no single confirmed number of days for all of these records or all
      jurisdictions. If we must retain information after your request, we will explain
      what remains, why, and the applicable duration or criteria for deletion. Clearing
      app data or uninstalling does not automatically delete support, RevenueCat or
      Google Play records. See <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy">RevenueCat’s Privacy Policy</a>
      {' '}and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/retention">Google’s retention information</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <h2 id="contact-title">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Legal developer / publisher:</strong> Sidhanshu Udawat<br />
      <strong>Privacy contact:</strong> Sidhanshu Udawat - <a href={deletionEmail}>{studio.email}</a>
    </p>
    <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-17">17 October 2026</time>.</p>
  </section>
</AppLayout>
